<title>SOUTH AFRICA: C.G. Smith year shr and div rises.</title>
<headline>C.G. Smith year shr and div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   156.5	 vs 132.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 56.0	  vs 48.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   799.8	 vs 597.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2,512.7     vs 1,943.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 767.7	 vs 698.6</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	 195.0 profit vs 68.4 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		  26,184.4    vs 23,602.2</p>
<p>Div payable Jan 10</p>
<p>on register Dec 6</p>
<p>Full name: C.G. Smith Ltd (Industrial Holding)</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  38.2	  vs 15.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the abnormal item arose mainly out of the profit on the change of interest in subsidiaries, associates and investments as well as the profit on disposal of land and buildings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
